{"timestamp":1774685097000,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"a4b98c32-c043-4dfd-ac1b-2ff3e23e3486","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXZcg2mmu5jnneamSf7Frv","payload":{"session_id":"a4b98c32-c043-4dfd-ac1b-2ff3e23e3486","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-c93e91a4/a4b98c32-c043-4dfd-ac1b-2ff3e23e3486.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/c93e91a4","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/c93e91a4/specs/issue-c93e91a4-adw-6-sdlc_planner-geo-tiered-cta-mode-toggle.md","content":"# Plan: Geo-tiered CTA mode toggle \u2014 settings-based buy/trial swap at hydrate level\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd a `ctaMode` settings flag (values: `default`, `buy-only`, `trial-only`) per geo/surface that suppresses conflicting CTAs at hydrate time in `web-components`. The toggle is authored in Studio and delivered through the existing MAS-IO settings pipeline \u2014 no card fragment content is modified. When a card's only CTA conflicts with the active mode and no paired CTA exists, a Learn More fallback link is rendered instead.\n\n## Task Description\n\nOn a per-locale/surface basis, GTM admins must be able to set `ctaMode` in Studio settings. The IO settings transformer delivers this flag in the fragment settings payload. During hydration in `web-components/src/hydrate.js`, `processCTAs` reads `settings.ctaMode` and:\n- `buy-only`: hides CTAs with `data-modal=\"twp\"` (trial), shows `data-modal=\"d2p\"` (buy)\n- `trial-only`: hides CTAs with `data-modal=\"d2p\"` (buy), shows `data-modal=\"twp\"` (trial)\n- `default`: no change (existing behavior)\n\nSuppressed CTAs are fully removed from the DOM (not just visually hidden). Single-CTA cards that conflict fall back to a `learnMoreUrl` anchor. A new `learnMoreUrl` field is added to the settings model for use as the fallback.\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Action | Reason |\n|------|--------|--------|\n| `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js` | Edit | Add `ctaMode` and `learnMoreUrl` to `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` |\n| `web-components/src/hydrate.js` | Edit | Add `processCtaMode()` function; call from `hydrate()` before `processCTAs` |\n| `web-components/src/constants.js` | Edit | Export `CTA_MODE` constant object (`DEFAULT`, `BUY_ONLY`, `TRIAL_ONLY`) |\n| `studio/src/settings/setting-name-map.js` | Edit | No change needed \u2014 auto-derives from `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` import |\n| `studio/src/settings/mas-settings.js` | Read/Verify | Confirm `ctaMode` select editor renders from `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` |\n| `web-components/test/unit/hydrate.test.js` | Edit | Add unit tests for `processCtaMode` |\n| `io/www/test/fragment/transformers/settings.test.js` | Edit | Add test for `ctaMode` extraction |\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Add `CTA_MODE` constants to `web-components/src/constants.js`\n\n- Add export:\n  ```js\n  export const CTA_MODE = {\n      DEFAULT: 'default',\n      BUY_ONLY: 'buy-only',\n      TRIAL_ONLY: 'trial-only',\n  };\n  ```\n- Validate: `node --check web-components/src/constants.js`\n\n### 2. Register `ctaMode` and `learnMoreUrl` in the settings transformer\n\n- In `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js`, append to `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS`:\n  ```js\n  { name: 'ctaMode', valueType: 'text', editor: 'select' },\n  { name: 'learnMoreUrl', valueType: 'text', editor: 'text' },\n  ```\n- `ctaMode` is a plain text field carrying one of the three CTA_MODE values; no special `propertyName` needed.\n- `learnMoreUrl` is a plain text URL stored as-is.\n- Validate: `node --check io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js`\n\n### 3. Implement `processCtaMode` in `web-components/src/hydrate.js`\n\n- Import `CTA_MODE` and `MODAL_TYPE_3_IN_1` from `./constants.js`.\n- Add function before `processCTAs`:\n\n  ```js\n  /**\n   * Suppresses CTAs that conflict with the active ctaMode setting.\n   * Fully removes conflicting CTAs from the DOM; falls back to a\n   * Learn More anchor if no compatible CTA remains.\n   * @param {object} fields - fragment fields\n   * @param {object} settings - resolved settings (may include ctaMode, learnMoreUrl)\n   */\n  export function processCtaMode(fields, settings) {\n      const mode = settings?.ctaMode;\n      if (!mode || mode === CTA_MODE.DEFAULT) return;\n\n      const ctas = fields.ctas;\n      if (!ctas) return;\n\n      // Parse the CTAs HTML string into a temporary container\n      const container = document.createElement('div');\n      container.innerHTML = ctas;\n\n      const links = [...container.querySelectorAll('a')];\n      if (!links.length) return;\n\n      const suppressModalType =\n          mode === CTA_MODE.BUY_ONLY\n              ? MODAL_TYPE_3_IN_1.TWP  // suppress trial CTAs\n              : MODAL_TYPE_3_IN_1.D2P; // suppress buy CTAs\n\n      links.forEach((link) => {\n          if (link.dataset.modal === suppressModalType) {\n              link.remove();\n          }\n      });\n\n      // If no compatible CTAs remain after suppression, use Learn More fallback\n      const remaining = container.querySelectorAll('a');\n      if (!remaining.length) {\n          const fallbackUrl = settings?.learnMoreUrl;\n          if (fallbackUrl) {\n              const learnMore = createTag('a', { href: fallbackUrl, class: 'secondary-link' }, 'Learn More');\n              container.append(learnMore);\n          } else {\n              // No fallback configured \u2014 leave fields.ctas empty (no CTA rendered)\n              fields.ctas = '';\n              return;\n          }\n      }\n\n      fields.ctas = container.innerHTML;\n  }\n  ```\n\n- In the `hydrate()` function, call `processCtaMode(fields, settings)` immediately before `processCTAs(fields, merchCard, mapping, variant)` (line 829):\n  ```js\n  processCtaMode(fields, settings);\n  processCTAs(fields, merchCard, mapping, variant);\n  ```\n\n- Validate: `node --check web-components/src/hydrate.js`\n\n### 4. Add unit tests for `processCtaMode`\n\n- In `web-components/test/unit/hydrate.test.js`, add test suite covering:\n  - `default` mode: fields.ctas unchanged\n  - `buy-only`: TWP link removed, D2P link retained\n  - `trial-only`: D2P link removed, TWP link retained\n  - Dual CTAs \u2014 both modes \u2014 correct one retained\n  - Single conflicting CTA with `learnMoreUrl` \u2192 replaced by Learn More anchor\n  - Single conflicting CTA without `learnMoreUrl` \u2192 `fields.ctas` set to `''`\n  - No `data-modal` attribute on CTAs \u2192 no change (pass-through)\n\n### 5. Add settings transformer test for `ctaMode`\n\n- In `io/www/test/fragment/transformers/settings.test.js` (or equivalent), add a test that:\n  - Constructs a settings fragment with a `ctaMode` entry set to `buy-only`\n  - Runs through `collectSettingEntries` + `applySettings`\n  - Asserts `fragment.settings.ctaMode === 'buy-only'`\n\n### 6. Verify Studio settings UI renders the new fields\n\n- Read `studio/src/settings/mas-settings.js` `renderSettingEditor()` method to confirm a `select` editor type is handled for `ctaMode`.\n- If `select` editor type is not handled, add a `case 'select':` rendering a `<sp-picker>` or equivalent with options `default`, `buy-only`, `trial-only` in the existing switch/if-else editor renderer.\n- Read `studio/src/settings/mas-setting-item.js` to confirm override dialog handles text editor for `learnMoreUrl`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- `settings.ctaMode = 'buy-only'` causes all fragments whose `fields.ctas` contains a `data-modal=\"twp\"` link to have that link removed from the rendered CTA slot before mount\n- `settings.ctaMode = 'trial-only'` causes all fragments whose `fields.ctas` contains a `data-modal=\"d2p\"` link to have that link removed before mount\n- When the only CTA in a card conflicts with the active mode and `settings.learnMoreUrl` is set, a `<a href=\"{learnMoreUrl}\" class=\"secondary-link\">Learn More</a>` is rendered in the CTA slot instead\n- When the only CTA conflicts and no `learnMoreUrl` is set, `fields.ctas` is empty and no CTA is rendered (no empty container)\n- `settings.ctaMode = 'default'` (or absent) leaves all CTAs unchanged \u2014 existing behavior is preserved\n- No content fragment data is written; the swap is purely a runtime mutation of `fields.ctas` before `processCTAs` is called\n- `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` in `settings.js` includes both `ctaMode` and `learnMoreUrl` entries, making them available to the Studio settings table automatically\n- `node --check` passes on all modified JS files\n- All new unit tests pass under `npm run test:ci` in both `io/www` and `web-components`\n\n## Validation Commands\n\n```sh\nnode --check web-components/src/constants.js\nnode --check web-components/src/hydrate.js\nnode --check io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js\ncd web-components && npm run test:ci\ncd io/www && npm run test:ci\n```\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXZcg2mmu5jnneamSf7Frv"}}
